"The `Module` class represents the top level structure present in LLVM "
"programs.  An LLVM module is effectively either a translation unit of the "
"original program or a combination of several translation units merged by the "
"linker.  The `Module` class keeps track of a list of {ref}`Function "
"<c_Function>`s, a list of {ref}`GlobalVariable <GlobalVariable>`s, and a "
"{ref}`SymbolTable <SymbolTable>`. Additionally, it contains a few helpful "
"member functions that try to make common operations easy."
